    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Andy Pages** positioned as our premier start (71.21). Facing Kochanowicz and his high-xERA (5.12), **Andy Pages** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill advantage and a coveted spot in the two-hole, making him our highest-ceiling asset today. Following closely, **Gunnar Henderson** (64.41) provides elite utility; despite a tough matchup against Fisher, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to his platoon advantage and Fisher\u2019s lethargic delivery, which creates prime conditions for stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical priority for our roster construction. **Sam Antonacci** (63.12) also earns a high-confidence nod, as his top-of-the-order role against Painter, combined with a strong 0.379 xwOBA, cements his floor in our daily rotation.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Nolan Schanuel**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 43.95 rating. While **Nolan Schanuel** projected as a viable candidate, he ultimately fell short of our efficiency threshold against a formidable Yamamoto, who suppresses production too effectively to justify taking a spot from our higher-upside starters. Meanwhile, caution is advised for **Dominic Smith** (42.18); while he avoids the bench, his matchup against Ashcraft is precarious. His score is bolstered by a platoon edge, but the SP skill disparity against him is significant. We are closely monitoring the status of **Jackson Merrill** (53.68) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.62), as both face elite defensive catchers today, adding a slight layer of risk to their steal potential. We will maintain discipline with our game caps, ensuring that sub-40 performers like **Coby Mayo** (38.80) and **Miguel Andujar** (35.72) remain on the bench to preserve our long-term Ottoneu flexibility.",
